<name>Steering Column</name>
<ttl id="1000U_S0017_745FR_T00AZ" variety="T00AZ">
<name>Electric Power Steering System</name>
<para id="RM000000W9S00DX" category="C" type-id="300E1" name-id="480XZ-00" from="200612">
<dtccode>C1511/11</dtccode>
<dtcname>Torque Sensor Malfunction 1</dtcname>
<dtccode>C1512/11</dtccode>
<dtcname>Torque Sensor Malfunction 2</dtcname>
<dtccode>C1513/11</dtccode>
<dtcname>Torque Sensor Deviation Excessive</dtcname>
<dtccode>C1514/11</dtccode>
<dtcname>Torque Sensor Power Supply Voltage Malfunction</dtcname>
<dtccode>C1517/11</dtccode>
<dtcname>Torque Hold Malfunction Continues</dtcname>
<subpara id="RM000000W9S00DX_01" type-id="33" category="03" proc-id="RM0550J___00005X400000">
<name>Function Description</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<ptxt>The power steering computer detects the steering effort based on the input signals from the torque sensor. As a fail-safe function, power assist is stopped while a torque sensor system malfunction is detected.</ptxt>
<table pgwide="1">
<tgroup cols="3">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="1.36in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="3.53in"/>
<colspec colname="COL3" colwidth="2.19in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>DTC NO</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Detection Item</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Inspection Area</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>C1511/11</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Torque sensor (TRQ1) signal malfunction or interruption</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry morerows="4" valign="middle">
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>Steering column assembly (with built-in torque sensor)</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Power Steering Computer Assembly</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>C1512/11</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Torque sensor (TRQ2) signal malfunction or interruption</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>C1513/11</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>When the deviation between torque sensor TRQ1 and TRQ2 is out of the specified range</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>C1514/11</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Torque sensor power supply voltage malfunction</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>C1517/11</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Temporary control due to torque sensor system malfunction continues for a long time</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</content5>
</subpara>
<subpara id="RM000000W9S00DX_02" type-id="32" category="03" proc-id="RM0550J___00005X500000">
<name>Wiring Diagram</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="C149379J04" width="7.106578999in" height="3.779676365in"/>
</figure>
</content5>
</subpara>
<subpara id="RM000000W9S00DX_03" type-id="51" category="05" proc-id="RM0550J___00005X600000">
<name>Inspection Procedure</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<atten3>
<ptxt>When the steering column assembly or power steering computer assembly has been replaced, perform torque sensor 0 point calibration and rotation angle sensor output calibration. (see <xref label="Seep01" href="RM0000024YB004X"/>)</ptxt>
</atten3>
</content5>
</subpara>
<subpara id="RM000000W9S00DX_04" type-id="01" category="01">
<name>Procedure</name>
<testgrp id="RM000000W9S00DX_04_0001" proc-id="RM0550J___00005X700000">
<testtitle>ECU Data Monitor Inspection (Torque Sensor 1 Output, Torque Sensor 2 Output)</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<test1>
<ptxt>Start the engine.</ptxt>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Using SST (TaSCAN), check "Torque Sensor Output 1" and "Torque Sensor Output 2" in the data monitor under each measurement condition. </ptxt>
</test1>
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09991-70200</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<spec>
<title>Standard</title>
<table pgwide="1">
<tgroup cols="3">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="2.69in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="2.17in"/>
<colspec colname="COL3" colwidth="2.22in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Measurement Condition</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Torque Sensor Output 1</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Torque Sensor Output 2</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Steering in neutral position (no load)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>2.3 to 2.7V</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>2.3 to 2.7V</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Steering turned right</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>2.5 to 3.8V</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>1.2 to 2.5V</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Steering turned left</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>1.2 to 2.5V</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>2.5 to 3.8V</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM000000W9S00DX_04_0005" fin="true">OK</down>
<right ref="RM000000W9S00DX_04_0002" fin="false">NG</right>
</res>
</testgrp>
